& [Implementation] is one feature-gated pure module
  + closed direction, root, limit, resource, recursion, definition, root-draft, universe, context, and typed-fault forms
  + fresh schemars generator per root and contract
  + same-direction definition merge only after canonical-byte equality
  + generated-Value compact canonical writer with sorted object keys and retained array order
  + local-reference extraction, target validation, lexical closure, visited-active cycle classification, and two authorized direct self cycles
  + domain-separated definition root and universe SHA-256 fingerprints using existing cantor_core sha256_bytes
  + atomic two-universe generation with no new dependency or external capability

& [MeasuredFootprint] is exact under schemars 1.2.2
  + input universe 53936 bytes, 80 definitions, 406 references, depth 8, 571 properties, 250 alternatives, 6 residuals
  + output universe 53846 bytes, 83 definitions, 398 references, depth 8, 567 properties, 271 alternatives, 6 residuals
  + prepare root 16955 bytes, run root 47285, verify root 51098, base response 52936, and preparation response 52936
  + pinned footprint preflight rejects insufficient lowered limits before schema generation; post-generation accounting detects any future upward drift

& [Identity] preserves intended use
  + base and preparation roots currently have equal raw schema digests
  + distinct root kinds schema ids and domain fingerprints prevent semantic collapse
  + input and output universes always have distinct contract fingerprints
  + supplied source revision is validated as lowercase 40-or-64 hexadecimal text and never represented as an observed Git fact

